 ### 3D Neural Texture Compression for TexF
-TexF compressed directly in 3D using the 3DNTC codec. It trains 3DNTC for 100k steps with MSE loss against TexF attributes. Batch sizes are 65,536 for K=2048 and 262,144 for K=4096. Adam learning rates start at 0.1 for latents and 0.005 for the decoder, following cosine decay to zero. The 3DNTC Hash Table Configuration is defined by dataset point $(s_1, s_2)$, feature channels $F$, and table sizes for 6 operating points. For 2048x2048 textures, table sizes increase with texture area up to fourfold. Decoding MACs for MLP widths $(2F + 18, 64, 48, 32, 16)$ cost $C = 144F + 6272$ MACs per query, including latent interpolation. This averages 8.96 KMACs on MPEG and 9.96 KMACs on AOM. Frame time on MPEG dataset is 10.8 ms (93 FPS); on AOM dataset: 23.1 ms (43 FPS), measured on RTX A6000 hardware. Attribute decoding time is 6.5 ms on MPEG and 15.8 ms on AOM. Per-query arithmetic cost is 8.96 KMACs on MPEG and 9.96 KMACs on AOM. Total encoding time is ~17 min on MPEG and ~28 min on AOM. Compared to NTC, TexF/3DNTC costs $C_{NTC} = 8192 + 8F_{NTC}$ MACs per query, averaging 8.28 KMACs for $F_{NTC} = (8, 12, 8, 12, 16)$ [S1, unofficial].
+TexF compressed directly in 3D using the 3DNTC codec [S1, unofficial]. It trains 3DNTC for 100k steps with MSE loss against TexF attributes [S1, unofficial]. Batch sizes are 65,536 for K=2048 and 262,144 for K=4096 [S1, unofficial]. Adam learning rates start at 0.1 for latents and 0.005 for the decoder, following cosine decay to zero [S1, unofficial]. The 3DNTC Hash Table Configuration is defined by dataset point $(s_1, s_2)$, feature channels $F$, and table sizes for 6 operating points [S1, unofficial]. For 2048x2048 textures, table sizes increase with texture area up to fourfold [S1, unofficial]. Decoding MACs for MLP widths $(2F + 18, 64, 48, 32, 16)$ cost $C = 144F + 6272$ MACs per query, including latent interpolation [S1, unofficial]. This averages 8.96 KMACs on MPEG and 9.96 KMACs on AOM [S1, unofficial]. Frame time on MPEG dataset is 10.8 ms (93 FPS); on AOM dataset: 23.1 ms (43 FPS), measured on RTX A6000 hardware [S1, unofficial]. Attribute decoding time is 6.5 ms on MPEG and 15.8 ms on AOM [S1, unofficial]. Per-query arithmetic cost is 8.96 KMACs on MPEG and 9.96 KMACs on AOM [S1, unofficial]. Total encoding time is ~17 min on MPEG and ~28 min on AOM [S1, unofficial]. Compared to NTC, TexF/3DNTC costs $C_{NTC} = 8192 + 8F_{NTC}$ MACs per query, averaging 8.28 KMACs for $F_{NTC} = (8, 12, 8, 12, 16)$ [S1, unofficial].
 
